  "narration": {
    "title": "Misiorowski Alone at the Top, Yankees Own the Staff",
    "intro": "It's a pitching day, and one name sits above the rest. Jacob Misiorowski is running a 1.68 ERA for Milwaukee, and the Yankees have quietly built the deepest staff in the game. Here's where the arms stand.",
    "staffs_lead": "The Yankees own the best rotation ERA at 3.35, with Detroit (3.44) right behind and the Dodgers (3.48) close after that. New York pairs it with a bullpen ranked second, so this is a staff good on both ends.",
    "bullpen_lead": "Boston's relief corps leads the way at 2.90, just ahead of the Yankees at 2.97. Milwaukee (3.33) rounds out the top three, giving the Brewers strength behind their front-line starters.",
    "arms_lead": "Jacob Misiorowski is in his own tier: a 1.68 ERA, a 0.76 WHIP, and a form score of 98, the only truly historic pace on the board. Cam Schlittler (86) and Yoshinobu Yamamoto (84) anchor the group behind him.",
    "risers_lead": "The week wasn't kind to a few good arms. Chase Burns slipped six points to a form of 71, Logan Webb fell five to 62, and Jos\u00e9 Soriano dropped five to 58 \u2014 cold stretches, not collapses, but worth noting."
  }
